content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22650 (motor replaced yesterday)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration of 4.8 mm/s falls in HF-300 Figure 3 Zone C (4.5 to 7.1 mm/s RMS, 'Restricted - plan maintenance'). It is above the Zone B long-term limit of 4.5 mm/s and below the Zone D stop threshold of 7.1 mm/s. The manual says to classify the highest reading from both bearing housings and act on that zone, so maintenance must be planned but an immediate stop is not required on this reading alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature of 70 C is exactly at the upper limit of the normal range (normal up to 70 C). It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip. Temperature is measured on the housing surface. No action is required on temperature alone, but there is no margin left and it must be monitored.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so there is no indication for mechanical seal replacement (leakage is the seal symptom in the troubleshooting table).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment between the new motor and the pump. The motor was replaced yesterday and high vibration appeared on restart. The manual requires laser alignment after any work that moves the motor, and lists misalignment as the first cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear, possibly made worse by running misaligned. This is a listed cause of high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the housing is already at the 70 C normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, take vibration velocity readings (mm/s RMS) on both bearing housings, drive end and non-drive end. Classify the highest reading against Figure 3. If any reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Record the bearing housing surface temperature. Raise an alarm at 80 C; trip/stop at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump and motor before working on the coupling or motor.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out a laser shaft alignment between the new motor and the pump to these tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Record as-found and as-left values.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Restart the pump, ensuring the casing is flooded and the Plan 11 seal flush is available (never run dry). Re-measure vibration on both bearing housings and housing temperature. The target is Zone B or better (4.5 mm/s RMS or below).",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration remains in Zone C after alignment, check NPSH/suction conditions for cavitation, then plan inspection of the bearings and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the bearings show wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair (section 5.3). Re-check alignment by laser afterwards, because that work moves the bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 - contingency only, if bearing inspection shows wear (replace as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 - contingency only, if bearing inspection shows wear (replace as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate (and drain where the pump is opened) before maintenance work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration on either bearing housing exceeds 7.1 mm/s RMS (Zone D - damage likely).",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature limits are alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The housing is currently at 70 C, the normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry; the seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Prime the pump before the post-alignment test run.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed for bearing or impeller inspection, it weighs 68 kg and lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency - bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians, only if inspection finds worn bearings.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal: the manual parts list specifies HF3-450 component seal with Table 5 torques. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes this for HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. For those pumps, do not fit HF3-450; use cartridge seal HF3-450B with a gland nut torque of 30 Nm (was 25 Nm), and replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. P-113 is serial HF3-22650, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies. No seal work is planned now (no leakage), but any future seal replacement on this pump must follow SB-2026-014, not the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 4.8 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on the bearing housing, as Figure 3 requires? What is the non-drive-end reading, given that the highest of both housings must be classified?",
    "Did the electrical contractor carry out or record a laser alignment after fitting the new motor? Are there as-left alignment values?",
    "What were the pre-motor-change baseline vibration and temperature readings for P-113, to confirm the change coincides with the motor swap?",
    "Does the replacement motor match the specification (1480 rpm, 55 kW, 400 V)? This is not confirmed in the report.",
    "The manual's Table 5 fastener torques, and any motor hold-down or coupling bolt torques, are not included in the evidence.",
    "The evidence gives no procedure for soft-foot checks, coupling inspection, or NPSH verification values.",
    "Is housing temperature trending upward since restart? Only a single 70 C value is given."
  ]
}
